\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The four-layer coordination stack. Each layer serves a different \emph  {whom} (machine, agents, operator, market). \textbf  {This paper owns the two lowest layers}: all of the substrate (the kernel) and the implemented carrier half of coordination (the message bus, stigmergic markers, commitments, the cryptographic authorization chain, the policy monitor); the coordination \emph  {semantics} (protocol state machines, the agent sandbox) and the whole legibility layer belong to companion papers (\emph  {The Legible Swarm}; \emph  {The Harbor Economy} owns the market rung). From the machine the substrate \emph  {assumes} only an advisory file lock, one clock, and a supervisor; upward it \emph  {provides} atomic TTL'd claims, a durable bus, the deontic split, and an audit log. Every companion paper builds on this one.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
