\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {3}The kernel as seven organs}{7}{section.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:organs}{{3}{7}{The kernel as seven organs}{section.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The kernel as \emph  {seven organs}, each a contract the daemon must hold for the layers above to be coherent. Six organs are, mechanically, just tables \emph  {with discipline} over a single shared file --- the \textbf  {substrate organ}, the single-writer transactional floor. The substrate's storage configuration \emph  {is} the kernel's durability claim (the I1a/I1b split, \S  \ref {sec:invariants}); a runtime-shim layer keeps the deployment and test SQLite bindings in step, and everything else is convenience built on top of it. Maturity grades (\textsf  {implemented} $\cdot $ \textsf  {partial} $\cdot $ \textsf  {specified} $\cdot $ \textsf  {proposed}) are per organ; note that the identity organ is implemented but \emph  {self-asserted}, the gap a cross-machine economy must eventually close with cryptographic identity.}}{8}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:swk-seven-organs}{{2}{8}{The kernel as \emph {seven organs}, each a contract the daemon must hold for the layers above to be coherent. Six organs are, mechanically, just tables \emph {with discipline} over a single shared file --- the \textbf {substrate organ}, the single-writer transactional floor. The substrate's storage configuration \emph {is} the kernel's durability claim (the I1a/I1b split, \S \ref {sec:invariants}); a runtime-shim layer keeps the deployment and test SQLite bindings in step, and everything else is convenience built on top of it. Maturity grades (\textsf {implemented} $\cdot $ \textsf {partial} $\cdot $ \textsf {specified} $\cdot $ \textsf {proposed}) are per organ; note that the identity organ is implemented but \emph {self-asserted}, the gap a cross-machine economy must eventually close with cryptographic identity}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {4}The substrate organ: one writer, one file}{8}{section.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:substrate}{{4}{8}{The substrate organ: one writer, one file}{section.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {4.1}The single-writer discipline}{9}{subsection.4.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The single-writer serialization, the cleanest thing about the layer. Dozens of command-line invocations and agents funnel through \emph  {one} writer --- the daemon, the sole holder of a read--write connection --- and SQLite's OS-level file lock plus a bounded busy-wait serialize all mutations. Because there is exactly one decider, there is no agreement to reach: the consensus impossibility of Fischer--Lynch--Paterson does not bite --- it is \emph  {sidestepped}, not solved, and on one machine the system is CP with a central coordinator. This is not a gap; it is the layer's defining discipline. The boundary is exact: the instant a \emph  {second} daemon shares this file, the assumption breaks and you have a distributed problem --- which belongs to the cross-machine economy layer, not here.}}{9}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:swk-single-writer}{{3}{9}{The single-writer serialization, the cleanest thing about the layer. Dozens of command-line invocations and agents funnel through \emph {one} writer --- the daemon, the sole holder of a read--write connection --- and SQLite's OS-level file lock plus a bounded busy-wait serialize all mutations. Because there is exactly one decider, there is no agreement to reach: the consensus impossibility of Fischer--Lynch--Paterson does not bite --- it is \emph {sidestepped}, not solved, and on one machine the system is CP with a central coordinator. This is not a gap; it is the layer's defining discipline. The boundary is exact: the instant a \emph {second} daemon shares this file, the assumption breaks and you have a distributed problem --- which belongs to the cross-machine economy layer, not here}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\newlabel{def:single-writer}{{4.1}{9}{Single-writer discipline}{definition.4.1}{}}
