\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {7}The communication organ: the bus, stigmergy, and two delegation chains}{14}{section.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:comm}{{7}{14}{The communication organ: the bus, stigmergy, and two delegation chains}{section.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The communication organ. The \textbf  {bus} envelope --- durable, ordered, at-least-once, history-cursored (\textsf  {implemented}) --- is the carrier \emph  {into which} the typed speech act is layered; the kernel ships the envelope, the coordination layer ships the semantics that ride inside it. \textbf  {Stigmergic markers} implement coordination with per-kind exponential decay computed both on a background tick and \emph  {at read time}, so the anti-blackboard-rot property is provided by the substrate rather than left to discipline. Finally, the figure fixes a dangerous naming collision --- never write bare ``delegation chain,'' it is two objects: the \emph  {authorization chain} is the hop-bound, attenuation-monotonic, anti-replay chain of signatures that proves \emph  {who authorized whom}; the \emph  {coordination lineage} is the coordination object that prevents ping-pong --- a different thing entirely, carried \emph  {inside} the authorization chain.}}{14}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:swk-comm-organ}{{6}{14}{The communication organ. The \textbf {bus} envelope --- durable, ordered, at-least-once, history-cursored (\textsf {implemented}) --- is the carrier \emph {into which} the typed speech act is layered; the kernel ships the envelope, the coordination layer ships the semantics that ride inside it. \textbf {Stigmergic markers} implement coordination with per-kind exponential decay computed both on a background tick and \emph {at read time}, so the anti-blackboard-rot property is provided by the substrate rather than left to discipline. Finally, the figure fixes a dangerous naming collision --- never write bare ``delegation chain,'' it is two objects: the \emph {authorization chain} is the hop-bound, attenuation-monotonic, anti-replay chain of signatures that proves \emph {who authorized whom}; the \emph {coordination lineage} is the coordination object that prevents ping-pong --- a different thing entirely, carried \emph {inside} the authorization chain}{figure.caption.12}{}}
