\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {8.3}Commitments: obligation with oracle-bound closure}{19}{subsection.8.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The commitment lifecycle with its oracle-bound closure gate. A commitment is a durable, \emph  {violable} promise (Cohen \& Levesque's persistent goal): it may end \emph  {done}, \emph  {abandoned}, or \emph  {superseded}. The load-bearing gate is Law~2 (I6): a transition to \emph  {done} is \emph  {refused} --- the promise stays open --- unless the agent supplies a reference drawn from the finite oracle vocabulary, re-verified by the daemon at closure time; free-text notes cannot close a promise. Law~1 (I5) closes the complementary Goodhart hole: the deadline is derived by the daemon from a scope policy --- the agent picks the \emph  {work}, never the \emph  {deadline}. That finite vocabulary is precisely the kernel's honesty boundary (OP-5): it can mechanically verify ``the test you named passed,'' never ``the refactor is good.''}}{19}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:swk-commitment-oracle}{{9}{19}{The commitment lifecycle with its oracle-bound closure gate. A commitment is a durable, \emph {violable} promise (Cohen \& Levesque's persistent goal): it may end \emph {done}, \emph {abandoned}, or \emph {superseded}. The load-bearing gate is Law~2 (I6): a transition to \emph {done} is \emph {refused} --- the promise stays open --- unless the agent supplies a reference drawn from the finite oracle vocabulary, re-verified by the daemon at closure time; free-text notes cannot close a promise. Law~1 (I5) closes the complementary Goodhart hole: the deadline is derived by the daemon from a scope policy --- the agent picks the \emph {work}, never the \emph {deadline}. That finite vocabulary is precisely the kernel's honesty boundary (OP-5): it can mechanically verify ``the test you named passed,'' never ``the refactor is good.''}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{prop:law1}{{8.1}{19}{Goodhart-resistance, Law 1}{property.8.1}{}}
\newlabel{prop:law2}{{8.2}{19}{Oracle-bound closure, Law 2}{property.8.2}{}}
\newlabel{alg:close}{{2}{20}{The commitment-closure oracle. Closure requires a reference from a finite vocabulary that the daemon re-verifies at closure time; free text is rejected by construction, not by inspection}{lstlisting.2}{}}
\@writefile{lol}{\contentsline {lstlisting}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The commitment-closure oracle. Closure requires a reference from a finite vocabulary that the daemon re-verifies at closure time; free text is rejected by construction, not by inspection.}}{20}{lstlisting.2}\protected@file@percent }
